-- 10. FOREIGN BUYERS (ss 235, 240, 243, 244)
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Am I a foreign individual` `none of these`
#ASSERT `Am I a foreign individual` `the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa`
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a foreign individual` `a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a foreign individual` `the holder of a permanent visa`)
-- A parent visa applicant within s 246(2)(b) is a specified foreign retiree but, being neither a citizen nor a permanent
-- resident, a foreign individual (s 235).
#ASSERT `Am I a foreign individual` `an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa`
-- A foreign individual alone buys an $800,000 house: AFAD 8% x 800,000 = 64,000; Chapter 2 duty at the general rate
-- (no specified resident, no home concession) 29,025. Transfer duty in all, the Chapter 2 duty and the AFAD (s 231(5),
-- (6)(a)): 29,025 + 64,000 = 93,025.
#ASSERT `How much additional foreign acquirer duty must I pay` 800000 800000 1 `none of these` TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 64000
#ASSERT `How much transfer duty must I pay before AFAD` `residential land` 800000 800000 0 TRUE `1 Aug 2026` TRUE `15 Aug 2026` `none of these` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 29025
#ASSERT `How much transfer duty must I pay` `residential land` 800000 800000 0 TRUE `1 Aug 2026` TRUE `15 Aug 2026` `none of these` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 93025
-- The same buyer, if the land is not AFAD residential land: no AFAD, 29,025.
#ASSERT `How much transfer duty must I pay` `residential land` 800000 800000 0 TRUE `1 Aug 2026` TRUE `15 Aug 2026` `none of these` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 29025
-- A foreign buyer of a $500,000 house with $20,000 of furniture (dutiable value 520,000): Chapter 2 duty at the general
-- rate on 520,000, 16,625; AFAD on the part for the AFAD residential land (s 244(2)(a)), 8% x 500,000 = 40,000;
-- 56,625 in all. The AFAD question, asked on the land alone, agrees: 40,000.
#ASSERT `How much transfer duty must I pay` `residential land` 520000 520000 20000 TRUE `1 Aug 2026` FALSE `15 Aug 2026` `none of these` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 56625
#ASSERT `How much additional foreign acquirer duty must I pay` 500000 500000 1 `none of these` TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 40000
-- A citizen (case 2's home at $600,000): no AFAD; transfer duty in all is the s 91 duty, 12,850.
#ASSERT `How much transfer duty must I pay` `residential land` 600000 600000 0 TRUE `1 Aug 2026` TRUE `15 Aug 2026` `an Australian citizen` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 12850
-- A New Zealand citizen on a special category visa buying a first home at $600,000: a permanent resident, so s 92 (nil)
-- and no AFAD: nil.
#ASSERT `How much transfer duty must I pay` `residential land` 600000 600000 0 TRUE `1 Aug 2026` TRUE `15 Aug 2026` `a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- A Subclass 405 retiree buying a first home: s 92 makes the Chapter 2 duty nil, but whether s 246 removes the AFAD is
-- not encoded, so the total is not covered.
#ASSERT `How much transfer duty must I pay` `residential land` 600000 600000 0 TRUE `1 Aug 2026` TRUE `15 Aug 2026` `the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `a specified foreign retiree: the s 246 exemption from AFAD is not encoded`
-- A trustee or company buyer: not covered, as for the Chapter 2 duty.
#ASSERT `How much transfer duty must I pay` `residential land` 800000 800000 0 FALSE `1 Aug 2026` FALSE `15 Aug 2026` `none of these` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `a buyer is a trustee or not an individual: the trust concessions and trust rules are not encoded`
-- Ana's case 6 house with a foreign spouse holding half: AFAD 8% x 600,000 x 0.5 = 24,000, not reduced by Ana's
-- concession (s 243); the transfer duty is the s 93 amount, 10,800.
#ASSERT `How much additional foreign acquirer duty must I pay` 600000 600000 0.5 `none of these` TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 24000
-- No AFAD for a permanent visa holder, or on land that is not AFAD residential land.
#ASSERT `How much additional foreign acquirer duty must I pay` 800000 800000 1 `the holder of a permanent visa` TRUE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `How much additional foreign acquirer duty must I pay` 800000 800000 1 `none of these` FALSE EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- A specified foreign retiree: the s 246 exemption is not encoded.
#ASSERT `How much additional foreign acquirer duty must I pay` 600000 600000 1 `the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa` TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `a specified foreign retiree: the s 246 exemption from AFAD is not encoded`
#ASSERT `How much additional foreign acquirer duty must I pay` 600000 600000 1 `an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa` TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `a specified foreign retiree: the s 246 exemption from AFAD is not encoded`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- 11. INTEREST AND PENALTY TAX (Administration Act ss 54, 58)
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- The s 54(5)(c)(ii) example: lodgement due 10 March, made 15 March: 5 days of noncompliance (11 to 15 March, the day
-- of compliance included); due date 17 April; 5 days before is 12 April; the start date is the day after, 13 April.
#ASSERT `From what day does unpaid tax interest run` `17 Apr 2027` `10 Mar 2027` `15 Mar 2027` EQUALS `13 Apr 2027`
-- Lodged on time (9 March): the start date is the day after the due date, 18 April.
#ASSERT `From what day does unpaid tax interest run` `17 Apr 2027` `10 Mar 2027` `9 Mar 2027` EQUALS `18 Apr 2027`
-- The s 54(7) example: $10,000 at 10% a year, 13 to 24 April inclusive (12 days): 10,000 x 0.10 x 12 / 365 = 32.8767,
-- "$32.87". On $2,000: 6.5753, so 6.57.
#ASSERT `How much unpaid tax interest will I owe` 10000 0.10 `13 Apr 2027` `24 Apr 2027` EQUALS 32.87
#ASSERT `How much unpaid tax interest will I owe` 2000 0.10 `13 Apr 2027` `24 Apr 2027` EQUALS 6.57
-- Paid before the start date: none.
#ASSERT `How much unpaid tax interest will I owe` 10000 0.10 `13 Apr 2027` `1 Mar 2027` EQUALS 0
-- s 58(2)(a): a default assessment of 20,025: 75% = 15,018.75; s 58(3) at most 20% more: 18,022.50.
#ASSERT (`What penalty tax can I be charged` TRUE 20025 20025 20025 TRUE)'s `penalty tax under s 58(2)` EQUALS 15018.75
#ASSERT (`What penalty tax can I be charged` TRUE 20025 20025 20025 TRUE)'s `the most it may be increased to under s 58(3)` EQUALS 18022.5
#ASSERT (`What penalty tax can I be charged` TRUE 20025 20025 20025 FALSE)'s `the most it may be increased to under s 58(3)` EQUALS 15018.75
-- s 58(1)(c), (2)(c): the first home buyer of section 9, reassessed from nil to 20,025 when the concession is clawed
-- back: 75% x 20,025 = 15,018.75 before any remission under s 60.
#ASSERT (`What penalty tax can I be charged` FALSE 20025 0 0 FALSE)'s `penalty tax under s 58(2)` EQUALS 15018.75
-- s 58(2)(d): original 20,000, lowest earlier reassessment 15,000, latest 18,000: 75% x 3,000 = 2,250.
#ASSERT (`What penalty tax can I be charged` FALSE 18000 20000 15000 FALSE)'s `penalty tax under s 58(2)` EQUALS 2250
-- Reassessed down from 20,000 to 18,000 with no earlier reassessment: no penalty tax.
#ASSERT (`What penalty tax can I be charged` FALSE 18000 20000 20000 FALSE)'s `penalty tax under s 58(2)` EQUALS 0

