-- 12. OBJECTIONS AND APPEALS (Administration Act ss 63-69)
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Notice given 1 September 2026: 60 days after is 31 October 2026 (29 days to 30 September, 31 more).
#ASSERT `By when must I object` `1 Sep 2026` EQUALS `31 Oct 2026`
-- Decision notice 15 January 2027: 60 days after is 16 March 2027 (16 to 31 January, 28 to 28 February, 16 more).
#ASSERT `Can I appeal or seek review, and by when` `15 Jan 2027` TRUE EQUALS `an appeal or application for QCAT review may be made up to and including` `16 Mar 2027`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal or seek review, and by when` `15 Jan 2027` FALSE EQUALS `not yet: the whole of the tax and late payment interest must be paid first, and the 60 days end on` `16 Mar 2027`

-- Object on day 30, decided on day 100, appeal on day 150 having paid: fulfilled. Not objecting at all is no breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `ss 63-69 -- the taxpayer may object within 60 days, the commissioner must decide, and the taxpayer may then appeal or seek review within 60 days, having paid` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `lodge an objection in writing, stating its grounds in detail, with copies of all relevant material` 30), (EVENT `the commissioner` `decide the objection and give the objector written notice of the decision` 100), (EVENT `the taxpayer` (`appeal to the Supreme Court or apply to QCAT for a review` TRUE) 150)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `ss 63-69 -- the taxpayer may object within 60 days, the commissioner must decide, and the taxpayer may then appeal or seek review within 60 days, having paid` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 61)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the obligation still pending: the commissioner MUST decide the objection (the Act sets no time)
#TRACE `ss 63-69 -- the taxpayer may object within 60 days, the commissioner must decide, and the taxpayer may then appeal or seek review within 60 days, having paid` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the taxpayer` DOES `lodge an objection in writing, stating its grounds in detail, with copies of all relevant material` AT 30
-- expect: still pending: the taxpayer DO appeal ... PROVIDED paid, WITHIN 40 more days (an appeal before paying does
-- not count)
#TRACE `ss 63-69 -- the taxpayer may object within 60 days, the commissioner must decide, and the taxpayer may then appeal or seek review within 60 days, having paid` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the taxpayer` DOES `lodge an objection in writing, stating its grounds in detail, with copies of all relevant material` AT 30
    PARTY `the commissioner` DOES `decide the objection and give the objector written notice of the decision` AT 100
    PARTY `the taxpayer` DOES `appeal to the Supreme Court or apply to QCAT for a review` FALSE AT 120

